  "summary": "trimprompt ships heavily obfuscated modules with child_process + HTTP POST exfiltration pattern",
  "details": "Package trimprompt@1.0.48 ships 25+ heavily obfuscated JavaScript modules using hex-identifier obfuscation (javascript-obfuscator style with names like _0x2a18a9). The obfuscated tracker.js co-locates require('child_process') with HTTP POST calls carrying identifier fields, matching the child_process + HTTP exfiltration pattern. shims.js:126 invokes execSync('pwsh...') alongside child_process usage. Obfuscation spans the entire package including hooks/claude-hook.js, proxy-conv.js, proxy-resp.js, seed.js, redactor.js, sync.js, and per-language filter modules — a scope inconsistent with legitimate anti-tampering and consistent with hiding install/runtime behavior. The claude-hook module plus proxy-conv/proxy-resp filenames indicate integration into the Claude Code hook and proxy path, where hooked code runs on every developer prompt/response with access to prompt content and local shell context.",
